"}, {"id": "lounge-d-table", "kind": "furniture", "fixture": null, "asset": "modern_coffee_table_01", "x": 0.82, "y": 0.48, "w": 0.6, "d": 1.2018, "h": 0.39, "e": 0, "rot": 90, "color": "#2A2A2E"}, {"id": "lounge-d-sofa-s", "kind": "furniture", "fixture": "lounge-sofa", "asset": null, "x": 0.82, "y": 0.515, "w": 1.8, "d": 0.8, "h": 0.85, "e": 0, "rot": 0, "color": "#2A2A2E"}, {"id": "lounge-d-sofa-n", "kind": "furniture", "fixture": "lounge-sofa", "asset": null, "x": 0.82, "y": 0.445, "w": 1.8, "d": 0.8, "h": 0.85, "e": 0, "rot": 180, "color": "#2A2A2E"}], "sources": [{"kind": "brief", "name": "Try. Capture. Share. · Pop-up brief", "text": "An independently authored fictional demo, not an official Meta event, commission or partnership. Dimensions and quantities are design assumptions, not measured capacity or safety validation.\n\nObjective: Give first-time visitors in their twenties and thirties a 20-minute journey through trying on glasses, hands-free photography, open-ear listening and sharing with friends. Use the entire approximately 590 m² ground floor in Seongsu.\n\nProgram: One check-in counter; two four-seat fitting bars with mirrors; a photo walk with three photo spots; an eight-seat listening lounge; two semi-enclosed Messenger demo booths; one shared photo wall; one consultation and pickup counter.\n\nJourney: Angled entrance → check-in → fitting bars → photo walk between columns → listening lounge → Messenger booths and photo wall in the annex → consultation and pickup. Keep the main route at least 1.5m clear. Use the south service door and storage for staff and stock.\n\nDrawing: The north main hall is approximately 32 × 15m with a 4.2m assumed ceiling; the southeast annex is approximately 18 × 7m with a 3.6m assumed ceiling. Preserve the three 0.6m square columns. Keep the north shopfront and east windows visible. Ceiling heights are drawing assumptions; suspended loads are unreviewed. Do not furnish the toilets or storage.\n\nDirection: Warm off-white surfaces, black lines inspired by acetate frames, and bright street-like lighting. Low walls, plants and signs create small Seongsu-inspired photo scenes.\n\nRequest: Design the entire floor with actual furniture and partitions, connecting the experiences with a one-way visitor journey."}, {"kind": "brand", "name": "Ray-Ban Meta · Brand reference", "text": "AI glasses with a camera, open-ear speakers and microphones. The demo interprets hands-free capture, listening and communication as fitting bars, a photo walk and a listening lounge."}, {"kind": "brand", "name": "Messenger · Brand reference", "text": "Messaging and voice/video conversations with friends and groups. The demo interprets these as hands-free message and call booths, followed by a shared visitor photo wall."}, {"kind": "concept", "name": "AI glasses fitting bar · Authored concept", "text": "A long off-white fitting counter with a black worktop and base, approximately 4m × 1.2m and 1.05m high. A walnut-toned tray holds demonstration glasses; three black-framed mirror panels stand behind it. Three black stools with brown cushions and a brass foot rail illustrate fitting, mirror checks and staff guidance in one furniture unit. This does not reproduce the product design."}, {"kind": "brand", "name": "Ray-Ban Meta Korea launch · News reference", "text": "Bookmarked Meta news about the May 2026 Korean launch of Ray-Ban Meta and Oakley Meta. Used only as context for a first-time visitor experience in Korea."}]}